 "prompt": "The repository at /testbed has a bug, described below. Fix it by changing the source code; do not modify or\nadd tests. When you are done, the project's existing test suite should pass.\n\n<issue>\nForeign key constraint parsing fails for CASCADE, RESTRICT, SET NULL, and SET DEFAULT actions\n\n#### Description\n\nWhen parsing foreign key constraints with referential actions like CASCADE, RESTRICT, SET NULL, or SET DEFAULT, the parser raises an \"Invalid key constraint\" error instead of properly handling these standard SQL actions.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nimport sqlglot\n\n# These should parse successfully but raise errors\nsql_statements = [\n    \"CREATE TABLE t (id INT, FOREIGN KEY (id) REFERENCES parent(id) ON DELETE CASCADE)\",\n    \"CREATE TABLE t (id INT, FOREIGN KEY (id) REFERENCES parent(id) ON UPDATE RESTRICT)\", \n    \"CREATE TABLE t (id INT, FOREIGN KEY (id) REFERENCES parent(id) ON DELETE SET NULL)\",\n    \"CREATE TABLE t (id INT, FOREIGN KEY (id) REFERENCES parent(id) ON UPDATE SET DEFAULT)\"\n]\n\nfor sql in sql_statements:\n    try:\n        parsed = sqlglot.parse_one(sql)\n        print(f\"\u2713 Parsed: {sql}\")\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f\"\u2717 Failed: {sql}\")\n        print(f\"  Error: {e}\")\n```\n\nExpected: All statements should parse successfully as these are valid SQL foreign key constraint actions.\n\nActual: Parser raises \"Invalid key constraint\" error for CASCADE, RESTRICT, SET NULL, and SET DEFAULT actions.\n</issue>\n",
